The RaiSim documentation site is built with VitePress (https://vitepress.dev)
from the Markdown pages in this directory:

* index.md                 home page (components in .vitepress/theme/components/home)
* sections/**/*.md         documentation pages, published as /sections/<page>.html
* .vitepress/config.mts    site configuration (navigation, search, math)
* .vitepress/sidebar.mts   documentation sidebar; add new pages here
* public/                  files served as they are (favicon, benchmark results)
* api/                     API reference for previews, generated from the Doxygen
                           XML by scripts/generate_api_docs.py (git-ignored)

Images and videos live in ../rsc/docs and are referenced with relative paths.
Use MP4 (H.264) for animations, not GIF, embedded as

  <video class="doc-video" src="../../rsc/docs/image/<name>.mp4" loop muted playsinline preload="metadata" aria-label="<what it shows>"></video>

without autoplay: the theme plays a clip only while it is on screen (and never
with reduced motion), so clips further down a page are not downloaded up front.
Mark a plot or diagram drawn on white with {.diagram} after the image (or
class="diagram" on an <img>): the dark theme then inverts it instead of showing
a white box. scripts/test_docs_figures.py fails for an unmarked one.
The example gallery (<ExampleGallery /> at the top of the Examples pages) shows
one category of sections/examples/gallery.json at a time, with a clip of each
example from ../rsc/docs/video/examples. Keep a category to about ten examples:
every clip of the chosen category plays at once. A category's icon is in
.vitepress/theme/exampleCategoryIcons.ts. image_generators/example_clips records
the clips and explains how to add an example.
Third-party assets: a page that shows a render of a CC BY 4.0 model (city
cars, off-road buggy and venue props, warehouse models, YCB objects,
MetalRoughSpheres) or of the TCP viewer's Flaticon icons links to
sections/AssetCredits.md, which credits them; add new ones there. Never publish
renders of assets licensed for non-commercial use only (such as DamagedHelmet)
or carrying third-party trademarks (AntiqueCamera). scripts/test_asset_credits.py
checks both.
Code from ../examples is included with
snippet imports, <<< @/../examples/<file>#<region>{cpp}, where the region is
marked with "// #region <name>" and "// #endregion <name>" comments.

Requirements: Node.js 18 or newer, Python 3 and Doxygen.

Preview while editing:

  npm ci
  npm run docs:dev

API pages come from the Doxygen XML of a docs build. Without them, links into
/api/ fail the preview's dead-link check. To generate them by hand:

  python3 scripts/generate_api_docs.py --xml <build>/docs/docs/doxygen/xml --out api

Full build: configure raisim2Lib with -DRAISIM_DOC=ON (or configure this
directory alone) and build the docs_site target. It writes nothing into this
directory. It copies the directory fresh to <build>/docs/site-src/docs on every
build, links ../rsc, ../examples and ../scripts next to the copy, runs Doxygen,
generates the API pages into the copy, installs the Node packages in
<build>/docs, builds the site into <build>/docs/docs/site and checks that every
internal link and #anchor resolves (scripts/check_links.py).
cmake/StageSiteSources.cmake does the copying. The links are directory
junctions on Windows: delete a build directory with Explorer, "rmdir /s" or
"cmake -E rm -rf", which remove a junction without entering it, not with
Windows PowerShell 5.1's Remove-Item -Recurse. update_doc.sh in the raisim
repository runs that build and publishes the site; pass --no-publish to only
build it.

Tests for the scripts: python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts

You can get the latest documentation from raisim.com.
